{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1188678-relics-ideas-101","id":1188678,"title":"Relics Ideas 101","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-22T15:14:18-08:00","id":1188678,"title":"Relics Ideas 101","content":"Let's start with something very easy.<br /> <br /> Name: Ace of clubs<br /> Aspect: a golfing bag containing a Golf Clubs X Legend Tier<br /> Effect and powers: Every club can be used as... a club. Doing bashings etcetc. But when you uncover the hood from the tophead of the club, something new will appear.<br /> <br /> Every club is an illusion of something also, maybe a gun, maybe a greatsword, maybe i bigger club or a bazooka. But everytime he use for an attack the weapon, this change back in a club again for X turns.<br /> <br /> The relic is pretty simple, a scion using this relic could be a strategic and very calm character. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T17:03:46-08:00","id":1188708,"title":"","content":"Name: Midas Gold Card<br /> Appearance: a golden credit card<br /> Motif: &quot;Endless wealth in your fingertips&quot;<br /> Effects: Gives access to the Prosperity purview. Can be freely charged for purchases of up to about a hundred dollars.<br /> Seems like a decent relic for non combative Theoi scions. The endless small purchases feature makes it a little easier for scions to get by without relying on their Paths when necessary.<br /> <br /> Name: Dreamer's Walking Staff<br /> Appearance: A walking staff that has been beautifully engraved with images from Manitou legends.<br /> Motif: Always walk towards your dreams<br /> Effects: Minor combat Enhancement. Gives access to the Journeys purview.<br /> <br /> An idea i had for a scion of Kitchi-Manitou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2472-trebius","name":"trebius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T02:37:47-08:00","id":1189170,"title":"","content":"I love the credit card, but i can't stop thinking about a shen's scion, son of the celestial burocracy, that hate this kind of relics because is not fair!<br /> <br /> <br /> Name: Nostalgic Thing<br /> Appearance: An old Polaroid Camera, always covered in dust<br /> Motif: Flash, give me death<br /> Effects: Access to Death/deception purview - this relic allows the scion to capture clearly and not in a blurry way, pics of ghosts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T13:21:54-08:00","id":1189989,"title":"","content":"Name: Neutonemesis<br /> Appearance: A trenchcoat<br /> Mechanically: Access to Fire &amp; Earth Purviews. +2l/+2B to Bulletproof vest template.<br /> This cloak feels very supple and flowing, almost as if it's a liquid strung together in your arms. But any sort of energy input results in it toughening up and absorbing/redistributing the blow. e.g. a hard stab would make it suddenly hard and near impiercable at the stab spot. Fire just gets absorbed as energy. A punch's energy makes the cloak harden where it is, before distributing the energy across the cloak like a ripple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23957-atlassniperman","name":"AtlasSniperman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T22:57:24-07:00","id":1195633,"title":"","content":"Name: Nacahuitl<br /> Appearance: A Renaissance era desk clock with a removable glass dome<br /> Mechanically: Access to Health Purview, + Unique three-dot power<br /> In the hands of someone with the Health purview, this clock provides access to all boons, as normal for an owned relic. However if the possesser does not have the health purview, or does not have access to the &quot;Heal/Inflict&quot; Boon, the clock can be made to produce the effect of said boon. By placing the clock atop a wound and using ones finger to move the hour hand forward in two circles across the face(and spending the requisite Willpower or Legend point), the clock heals the wound as if sufficient time had passed for it to heal naturally. If someone who already has the &quot;Heal/Inflict&quot; Boon uses the clock in this way, they may spend Legend points equal to the Legend score of whom is being healed, instead of the Willpower point normally required.<br /> Drawback: While an excellent source of healing, this clock has one major detriment; Any person healed by the clock is aged as would be required to heal the damage naturally. This can lead to an early grave if overused, though characters with the &quot;Eternal Youth&quot; Knack needn't worry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23957-atlassniperman","name":"AtlasSniperman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T07:10:30-07:00","id":1198634,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Shinobi Elder Sword</b> (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): Forged from the shurikens of fallen Shinobu by one of the last Shinobu Elders, this sword latches itself to anyone that defeats its previous user. The sword grants its user the Darkness purview, as well as being faster (-1 Speed), and more deadly than a standard ninjato (+1L). But what sets this sword apart from its counterparts is its ability not generate sound by itself, meaning that any action performed with it is silent, along with the fallout of those actions.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24027-r_pon217","name":"R_Pon217","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24027_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}